CORE CONSTANTS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Omega_ZS = W(1) = 0.56714...
  Lambert W fixed point: W . e^W = 1, i.e. the fixed point of f(x) = e^{-x}.
  Confirmed independently in 6 formula families: spectral (Berry-Keating),
  algebraic, galactic baryonic fraction (SPARC), logarithmic, and the 6
  fractal-orbit formulas below all converge here as their natural
  equilibrium constant.

d* = Omega_ZS / ln(10) = 0.24631...
  "The Zero Definer" -- smallest natural unit in universal native space,
  the boundary below which no algebraic definition can occur. d* x ln(10)
  = Omega_ZS.
  Four measured faces (not four different values -- four shadows of one
  point):
    d*_spec  ~ 0.24600   Berry-Keating spectral gap (SPARC-observed)
    d*_taut  = 0.24631   Lambert W, exact
    d*_RG    = OPEN      renorm-group fixed point under CD tower iteration
    d* x ln(10) = 0.56714  = Omega_ZS

GAP = Omega_ZS - d*_spec x ln(10) ~ 1/(1000 sqrt(2)) ~ 7.07e-4
  The Yang-Mills mass gap analogue in the semantic field. 1/sqrt(2) factor
  = sigma=1/2 symmetry. The 10^3 factor is UNRESOLVED -- no first-
  principles derivation yet. State this as open when it comes up.

V(n) = pi^(n/2) / Gamma(n/2 + 1)          [n-ball volume]
  Peaks at n* ~ 5.257 (BAO acoustic scale). V(16) ~ d* (approximates, not
  equals -- the geometry approximates the algebra, the algebra is exact).

