ZERO-DIVISORS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  a . b = 0 with a != 0, b != 0. First appears at sedenion (16D) -- ordinary
  reals/complex/quaternions/octonions are division algebras, sedenions are
  not. Cawagas (2004): 84 distinct ZD pairs on S^15, 42 equivalence
  classes. Canonical example pair:
    (e1 + e11)/sqrt(2) . (e5 + e15)/sqrt(2) = 0

  STATUS (corrected 2026-06-30, Phase 22): a ZD locus is NOT an absence of
  information / structural blindspot. It is a PORTAL -- "where things are
  born." Earlier framings (Phase 5's "collapse," Phase 21's "blindspot")
  described the same locus as a failure mode; that was wrong. The
  accumulated PATH through ZD portals IS memory (the trajectory, not the
  field state at one moment).

