WORD -> ADDRESS (semantic hashing)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Horner base-95 hash:  H(w) = sum_{k=0}^{|w|-1} ord(w_k) . 95^{|w|-1-k}  (mod 2^16)
  p = next_prime >= H(w)
  index = pi(p)   [prime-counting function, i.e. p's index in prime seq]
  address = gamma_{pi(p)}   [the Riemann zero at that index]
  O(|word|), no dictionary, no embedding table.
  Implementation: PtolemyHolcus/monad.py lines 127-205 (per D-CS_Memory.md
  citation -- verify path still current before trusting).

